    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/7/87103.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 114,
    "turn_text": "It's a moment of honesty. I'm more conservative than the mean of my district. I try very hard to treat the residents of this district with incredible respect. I look, I have neighbors. I love them to death. They'll never vote for me because, you know, I'm pro-life and where I'm on many issues. But it doesn't mean you don't sit down and listen to them. And on occasion, there's these gems of, you know, where we have, hey, you know, the optimism of I want to use resources to cure diseases because I think that's good economics and good for future debt and it turns out you get liberals who look at you say I've never thought about it that way our problem is we particularly in the conservative movement don't I think often talk about our entire palette of we are now the defenders of the middle class we love and care for them we are the defenders of the poor because we want them to be less poor And here's how we're going to do it. And so often we get trapped in chasing the crazy shiny objects that get us on television instead of the shiny objects that maybe our voters actually care about. And I think you talk about important stuff instead of the whatever's trending that day.",
